Spec: SpecDD Section Completion Model

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Decide when section name completion is available and create section lookup variants.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDSectionCompletion.kt

Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/SpecDDLanguageFacts.kt
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/completion/SpecDDSectionCompletionBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Return no completion result when the caret offset is outside the text.
  Return no completion result when the current line is indented before the caret.
  Return no completion result when the current line prefix contains non-section-label syntax.
  Return no completion result when the current line prefix matches no known section label.
  Return all known section labels for an empty unindented line prefix.
  Return matching known section labels for a partial unindented line prefix.
  Match partial prefixes case-insensitively.
  Preserve the original known section label spelling in completion variants.
  Expose lookup strings as section header text ending with `: `.
  Keep the model independent from editor registration and plugin metadata.

Must not:
  Depend on validation, highlighting, documentation, or structure view code.
  Report validation diagnostics.
